WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.948
In spring 1989, protests appeared in Beijing.

00:00:03.948 --> 00:00:07.984
Students and citizens took to the streets to voice their demands.

00:00:07.984 --> 00:00:11.424
University students rode bicycles through the long streets.

00:00:11.424 --> 00:00:14.597
Many people gathered in Tiananmen Square.

00:00:14.597 --> 00:00:17.138
In other cities, people also came out in response.

00:00:17.138 --> 00:00:22.064
People in the square shared food and water with each other.

00:00:22.064 --> 00:00:24.555
In early June, the situation changed overnight.

00:00:24.555 --> 00:00:27.900
The military suppressed the protests by force.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:31.661
The crackdown caused civilian deaths and injuries.

00:00:31.661 --> 00:00:35.490
Many families lost loved ones from then on.

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:38.940
White flowers were placed beside candlelight.

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:42.948
Later, people used candlelight to commemorate this history.

00:00:42.948 --> 00:00:46.180
On this day each year, candles burn quietly.

00:00:46.392 --> 00:00:50.122
In the silent crowd, only candle flames flickered.

00:00:50.122 --> 00:00:54.161
This history is still remembered by many people today.

00:00:54.161 --> 00:00:57.535
People hope the truth and remembrance will not disappear.
